  "id": "iowa-gambling-task",
  "term": "Iowa Gambling Task",
  "definition": "The Iowa Gambling Task is a psychology task used to study decision making under ambiguity and risk by having a person repeatedly choose from four card decks that differ in short-term rewards and long-term losses. As feedback is given after each choice, it assesses how well someone learns from outcomes to favor options with better long-term results over immediately tempting but disadvantageous ones.",
